course: dictionary
lesson: 5834
title: Majesty: grand and royal
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Majesty is a noun with two meanings. The first is great beauty, size and power that makes people feel wonder: «the majesty of the mountains» means the mountains look grand, huge and amazing. You can feel majesty about nature, with no royal people in sight.
explain: The second meaning is about kings and queens. «Your Majesty», «His Majesty» and «Her Majesty» are polite ways to speak to or about a king or queen. In one old story, Alice says «please your Majesty» to a queen, and the word shows respect.
explain: Use the context to choose the meaning. If the sentence describes a waterfall, an eagle or a castle, it means the first meaning. If someone is speaking politely to a ruler, it means the second. Ask yourself: is this about something grand in nature, or about a royal person?
fact: Majesty means great beauty, size and power that makes people feel wonder.
fact: «The majesty of the mountains» means the mountains look grand and amazing.
fact: «Your Majesty» is a polite way to speak to a king or queen.
fact: «His Majesty» and «Her Majesty» are polite ways to talk about a king or queen.
fact: In descriptive writing, majesty shows something grand, such as a waterfall, an eagle or a castle.
exercise: «The waterfall fell over the cliff with great majesty.» What does majesty mean here? | Lots of rain on a cold day | Being very late | *Great beauty and power that makes people feel wonder | A small, quiet noise
exercise: Servants bowed low and said, «Yes, Your Majesty.» Who were they speaking to? | A teacher in a classroom | *A king or queen | A farmer with a tractor | A pirate captain
exercise: «The majesty of the mountains» means the mountains look | *Grand and amazing | Small and dull | Old and broken | Wet and cold
test: «The eagle spread its wings, and the children stopped to watch its majesty.» What does majesty mean here? | A type of rope | Silly and funny | Very hungry | *Great beauty and power that makes people feel wonder
test: Tom bows and says, «Good morning, Your Majesty.» Why does he say this? | It is a secret code | It means he is late for school | It means he wants his lunch | *It is a polite way to speak to a queen or king
exam: Which sentence uses majesty in the royal sense? | «The eagle's majesty filled the whole sky.» | *«Please speak to His Majesty with respect.» | «The majesty of the cliffs took my breath away.» | «We stood in awe at the majesty of the sunset.»
